        "text": "Between the 6th and 4th centuries BCE, the kingdom of Magadha outpaced rival Mahajanapadas (Kosala, Vatsa, Avanti) to emerge as India's first pan-regional imperial nucleus. Ruled successively by the Haryanka, Shishunaga, and Nanda dynasties, Magadha built a massive standing army, perfected riverine warfare, and laid the administrative groundwork for the Mauryan Empire."
