        "text": "The Satavahanas (known as Andhras in the Puranas) held sway over the Deccan plateau (Maharashtra, Andhra Pradesh, and northern Karnataka) for over four centuries (c. 1st Century BCE to 3rd Century CE). Founded by Simuka with capitals at Pratishthana (Paithan) and Dhanyakataka (Amaravati), the Satavahanas pioneered royal land grants (Agraharas), built rock-cut Buddhist chaityas across the Western Ghats, and fostered Indian Ocean maritime commerce."
