        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Following the collapse of the Gupta Empire under Huna invasions, political unity fragmented into regional successor kingdoms: the Pushyabhutis of Thanesar, the Maukharies of Kanauj, the Maitrakas of Vallabhi, and the Gaudas of Bengal. Harsha Vardhana (606–647 CE) reunited northern India, shifted his imperial capital to Kanauj, patronized Mahayana Buddhism, and hosted Chinese pilgrim Xuanzang (Hiuen Tsang)."
