        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Between 1767 and 1849, the British East India Company dismantled the premier military powers of the subcontinent—Mysore, the Maratha Confederacy, and the Sikh Empire—through a combination of military campaigns and diplomatic instruments of paramountcy. Guided by Lord Wellesley's Subsidiary Alliance and Lord Dalhousie's Doctrine of Lapse, the Company subjugated princely states, erasing Indian sovereignty across South Asia."
