        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "On the eve of independence in August 1947, India faced the existential threat of Balkanization into over 565 autonomous princely fiefdoms following the lapse of British Paramountcy. Through the consummate diplomatic finesse, statesmanship, and firm resolve of Deputy Prime Minister Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel and States Secretary V.P. Menon, the princely states were successfully integrated into the Indian Union, while the Constituent Assembly under Dr. B.R. Ambedkar framed the world's most comprehensive written democratic constitution."
