        "text": "The British colonization of Andhra unfolded in stages: the acquisition of the Northern Circars from the Nizam in 1765–1768, followed by the acquisition of the Ceded Districts (Rayalaseema) in 1800. Plagued by ruthless revenue extortion and devastating famines (notably the Guntur Famine of 1832), the coastal Andhra delta was rescued from economic ruin by the visionary hydraulic engineering of Sir Arthur Cotton, whose anicuts on the Godavari and Krishna transformed coastal Andhra into the granary of South India."
