        "text": "The Indian subcontinent exhibits extraordinary geomorphological diversity shaped by plate tectonics—from the collision of the Indian and Eurasian plates giving birth to the young fold mountains of the Himalayas, to the ancient Archean peninsular shield. Andhra Pradesh is characterized by three distinct physiographic provinces: the Coastal Plains along its 974 km coastline, the dissected Eastern Ghats, and the semi-arid Rayalaseema plateau."
