        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The climate of India is classified as Tropical Monsoon, driven by differential heating between the Indian Ocean and the Asian landmass, seasonal reversals of low-level planetary winds, and upper-tropospheric jet streams. Andhra Pradesh experiences a transitional climatic regime benefiting from both the Southwest Monsoon (June–September) and the retreating Northeast Monsoon (October–December), while remaining acutely vulnerable to devastating post-monsoon Bay of Bengal tropical cyclones."
