        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The constitutional machinery at the state level mirrors the parliamentary structure of the Union. Headed by the Governor as the representative of the Union and constitutional executive, real authority resides in the Chief Minister and Council of Ministers responsible to the Legislative Assembly (Vidhan Sabha). The office of the Governor remains a sensitive focal point of Indian federalism, particularly regarding discretionary powers and recommendations under Article 356."
