        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The Indian Constitution establishes an integrated, single judicial pyramid with the Supreme Court at the apex, exercising supreme appellate authority, constitutional interpretation, and the defense of fundamental rights. Characterized by judicial independence guaranteed through tenure security and the judge-led Collegium appointment system, the Indian judiciary has pioneered proactive constitutional tools like Judicial Review, Judicial Activism, and Public Interest Litigation (PIL)."
