        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "The rapid digitalization of India's socio-economic fabric requires a robust legal architecture balancing cybersecurity, privacy, and economic dynamism. The Information Technology Act 2000, bolstered by the landmark Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023, protects digital rights and operationalizes the fundamental right to privacy established in the Puttaswamy judgement. Concurrently, India's fiscal framework harmonizes revenue mobilization across direct income taxation and the unified Goods and Services Tax (GST) cooperative federal regime."
