        "text": "Pollution control and ecosystem restoration are paramount for safeguarding public health, environmental justice, and ecological resilience. Regulated by the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) and State Pollution Control Boards (APPCB) under the Water Act 1974 and Air Act 1981, India's environmental apparatus enforces stringent mandates including the National Clean Air Programme (NCAP), Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) across plastic and electronic waste, the Coastal Regulation Zone (CRZ 2019) framework, and Ramsar wetland conservation."
