          "Q4. If 2^(x - 1) + 2^(x + 1) = 320, find the value of x.\n(a) 5\n(b) 6\n(c) 7\n(d) 8\nCorrect Answer: (c) 7 [Explanation: 2^(x-1) + 2^(x+1) = 2^x * (1/2 + 2) = 2^x * (5/2) = 320 => 2^x = (320 * 2) / 5 = 64 * 2 = 128 = 2^7 => x = 7.]",
