    "topic_title": "Harsha Vardhana, Kanauj Assembly & Post-Gupta Formations",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. According to Xuanzang's accounts, into how many equal shares did Emperor Harsha divide the royal revenues of the state?\n(a) Two parts\n(b) Three parts\n(c) Four parts\n(d) Six parts\nCorrect Answer: (c) Four parts [Explanation: Xuanzang recorded that Harsha divided state revenues into four quarters: one for state administration, one for salaries of public servants, one for rewarding intellectual talent, and one for charity to religious orders.]"
