    "raw_text": "Q1. The famous Uttaramerur Inscriptions, which provide a detailed constitutional blueprint of village assemblies and committee elections, belong to the reign of:\n(a) Vijayalaya\n(b) Parantaka I\n(c) Rajaraja I\n(d) Rajendra I\nCorrect Answer: (b) Parantaka I [Explanation: The two landmark inscriptions at Uttaramerur in Kanchipuram district were issued in the 12th and 14th regnal years of Chola King Parantaka I (919 and 921 CE).]"
