    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q2. Which Chola monarch assumed the proud title 'Gangaikondachola' (Conqueror of the Ganga) and founded a new imperial capital to commemorate his northern campaign?\n(a) Rajaraja I\n(b) Rajendra I\n(c) Kulottunga I\n(d) Rajadhiraja I\nCorrect Answer: (b) Rajendra I [Explanation: After his victorious military expedition to the banks of the River Ganga defeating Mahipala of Bengal, Rajendra I assumed the title 'Gangaikondachola' and founded Gangaikondacholapuram.]"
