    "topic_title": "Bhakti & Sufi Movements: Philosophies, Saints & Cultural Synthesis",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q3. The poetic compositions and philosophical dialogues of Saint Kabir are predominantly compiled in which sacred collection?\n(a) Ramcharitmanas\n(b) Bijak\n(c) Sursagar\n(d) Padavali\nCorrect Answer: (b) Bijak [Explanation: The 'Bijak' (compiled by his disciple Bhagodas) is the foundational scripture containing Kabir's Dohas, Sakhis, and Shabads criticizing external religious dogmas.]"
