    "raw_text": "Q1. Which heroic sepoy of the 34th Bengal Native Infantry fired at his British commanding officers at Barrackpore on 29 March 1857, igniting the 1857 uprising?\n(a) Bakht Khan\n(b) Mangal Pandey\n(c) Ishwar Pandey\n(d) Mata Din\nCorrect Answer: (b) Mangal Pandey [Explanation: Sepoy Mangal Pandey of the 34th BNI revolted at Barrackpore parade ground on 29 March 1857 protesting greased cartridges, becoming the opening martyr of the revolt.]"
