    "raw_text": "Q2. The octogenarian Rajput zamindar who led the 1857 armed resistance in Jagdishpur (Arrah, Bihar) and inflicted repeated defeats on British forces was:\n(a) Amar Singh\n(b) Kunwar Singh\n(c) Pir Ali\n(d) Khan Bahadur Khan\nCorrect Answer: (b) Kunwar Singh [Explanation: Babu Kunwar Singh, the 80-year-old chieftain of Jagdishpur in Bihar, displayed extraordinary military leadership and guerrilla warfare against British detachments.]"
