    "topic_title": "The Revolt of 1857: Causes, Key Leaders, Suppression & Aftermath",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q4. Which British monarchial declaration, read out by Lord Canning at the Allahabad Darbar on 1 November 1858, announced the direct assumption of Indian governance by the British Crown?\n(a) Charter Act of 1858\n(b) Queen Victoria's Proclamation\n(c) Royal Titles Act\n(d) Government of India Manifesto\nCorrect Answer: (b) Queen Victoria's Proclamation [Explanation: Lord Canning read Queen Victoria's Proclamation at Allahabad on 1 November 1858, guaranteeing respect for ancient rights and pledging no further territorial annexations.]"
