    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Which commission was constituted immediately after the 1857 Revolt to reorganize the Indian Army and ensure higher ratios of European troops?\n(a) Hunter Commission\n(b) Peale Commission\n(c) Fraser Commission\n(d) Welby Commission\nCorrect Answer: (b) Peale Commission [Explanation: The Peale Commission (1858) recommended maintaining a strict 1:2 European-to-Indian soldier ratio in Bengal and 1:3 in Madras/Bombay, pioneering the 'martial vs non-martial' recruitment doctrine.]"
