    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q3. Who accompanied Bhagat Singh in throwing non-lethal smoke bombs and leaflets ('To make the deaf hear') into the Central Legislative Assembly in Delhi on 8 April 1929?\n(a) Rajguru\n(b) Batukeshwar Dutt\n(c) Sukhdev\n(d) Jatin Das\nCorrect Answer: (b) Batukeshwar Dutt [Explanation: Bhagat Singh and Batukeshwar Dutt hurled non-lethal bombs into the empty benches of the Central Legislative Assembly to protest the repressive Public Safety and Trade Disputes Bills.]"
