    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Revolutionary freedom fighter Jatin Das attained martyrdom after an epic 63-day hunger strike in Lahore Central Jail in September 1929 demanding:\n(a) Release of all political prisoners\n(b) Civil rights and political prisoner status for undertrial revolutionaries\n(c) Commutation of Bhagat Singh's death sentence\n(d) Immediate repeal of the Rowlatt Act\nCorrect Answer: (b) Civil rights and political prisoner status for undertrial revolutionaries [Explanation: Jatin Das died on 13 September 1929 following a 63-day fast demanding humane prison conditions, hygienic food, and dignified status as political prisoners rather than common criminals.]"
