    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q1. Which local peasant leader from Bihar persistently persuaded Mahatma Gandhi at the 1916 Lucknow Congress to visit Champaran and investigate the grievances of indigo ryots?\n(a) Raj Kumar Shukla\n(b) Brajkishore Prasad\n(c) Anugrah Narayan Sinha\n(d) J.B. Kripalani\nCorrect Answer: (a) Raj Kumar Shukla [Explanation: Raj Kumar Shukla, an indigo cultivator from Champaran, persistently urged Gandhi to visit Bihar, leading to Gandhi's historic First Civil Disobedience at Champaran in 1917.]"
