    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q2. Following the gruesome Jallianwala Bagh Massacre on 13 April 1919, who renounced his British Knighthood in an impassioned protest letter to Viceroy Lord Chelmsford?\n(a) Mahatma Gandhi\n(b) Rabindranath Tagore\n(c) Sir Syed Ahmad Khan\n(d) Subhas Chandra Bose\nCorrect Answer: (b) Rabindranath Tagore [Explanation: Rabindranath Tagore renounced his Knighthood in May 1919, declaring that the time had come when badges of honour make our shame glaring in the incongruous context of suffering.]"
