    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q3. The Non-Cooperation program was formally endorsed and the constitution of the Indian National Congress reorganized on linguistic lines at which historic annual session in December 1920?\n(a) Calcutta Special Session\n(b) Nagpur Annual Session\n(c) Ahmedabad Session\n(d) Gaya Session\nCorrect Answer: (b) Nagpur Annual Session [Explanation: The December 1920 Nagpur Congress session, presided over by C. Vijayaraghavachariar, ratified the Non-Cooperation program and reorganized Congress committees along linguistic boundaries.]"
