    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q4. Following the violent death of 22 policemen at Chauri Chaura on 4 February 1922, Mahatma Gandhi suspended the Non-Cooperation Movement through which historic resolution?\n(a) Lucknow Resolution\n(b) Bardoli Resolution\n(c) Delhi Manifesto\n(d) Wardha Resolution\nCorrect Answer: (b) Bardoli Resolution [Explanation: The Congress Working Committee met at Bardoli on 12 February 1922 and passed the Bardoli Resolution formally terminating the civil disobedience and Non-Cooperation movement.]"
