    "topic_title": "Civil Disobedience: Dandi March, Round Table Conferences & Poona Pact",
    "subject_title": "History and Culture of India",
    "raw_text": "Q5. The historic Poona Pact, signed on 24 September 1932 between representatives of caste Hindus and the Depressed Classes, replaced separate electorates with:\n(a) Universal adult franchise without reservations\n(b) Joint electorates with reserved seats for Depressed Classes\n(c) Proportional representation by single transferable vote\n(d) Nomination by the Governor-General\nCorrect Answer: (b) Joint electorates with reserved seats for Depressed Classes [Explanation: The Poona Pact discarded separate electorates in favor of joint electorates with reserved seats, increasing legislative seats for the Depressed Classes from 71 to 148.]"
