    "topic_title": "Agriculture & Irrigation in Andhra Pradesh: Cropping Systems & Agrarian Economy",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q3. The famous 'Banganapalle Mango' (Benishan), which was granted a prestigious Geographical Indication (GI) tag, originates from which district of Andhra Pradesh?\n(a) Chittoor\n(b) Nandyal / Kurnool\n(c) Krishna\n(d) Kadapa\nCorrect Answer: (b) Nandyal / Kurnool [Explanation: Banganapalle mangoes, celebrated for their fiberless pulp and sweet aroma, originate from the Banganapalle princely estate in Kurnool/Nandyal district.]"
