    "topic_title": "Mineral & Energy Resources of India & AP: Barytes, Bauxite, Uranium & KG Basin",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q1. The world's largest single deposit of bedded barytes, accounting for over 97% of India's total reserves, is located at which site in Andhra Pradesh?\n(a) Tummalapalle\n(b) Mangampeta\n(c) Bheemunipatnam\n(d) Macherla\nCorrect Answer: (b) Mangampeta [Explanation: Mangampeta in YSR Kadapa district possesses the world's largest known bedded barytes deposit, mined open-cast by the APMDC.]"
