    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The massive domestic uranium deposit discovered by the Atomic Minerals Directorate and mined by UCIL is situated at Tummalapalle in which district of AP?\n(a) Kurnool\n(b) YSR Kadapa\n(c) Anantapur\n(d) Chittoor\nCorrect Answer: (b) YSR Kadapa [Explanation: Tummalapalle in YSR Kadapa district holds one of the largest uranium reserves in the world, with confirmed deposits exceeding 150,000 tonnes.]"
