    "topic_title": "Mineral & Energy Resources of India & AP: Barytes, Bauxite, Uranium & KG Basin",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q3. Which major deepwater offshore sedimentary basin in coastal Andhra Pradesh holds vast natural gas reserves, including the historic KG-D6 gas field?\n(a) Cauvery Basin\n(b) Krishna-Godavari (KG) Basin\n(c) Mahanadi Basin\n(d) Cambay Basin\nCorrect Answer: (b) Krishna-Godavari (KG) Basin [Explanation: The Krishna-Godavari (KG) offshore basin holds India's premier deepwater natural gas and crude reserves, operated by ONGC and Reliance.]"
