    "topic_title": "Mineral & Energy Resources of India & AP: Barytes, Bauxite, Uranium & KG Basin",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q4. Heavy mineral beach sands along the coastal belt of Srikakulam and Visakhapatnam contain rich concentrations of 'Monazite', which is the primary source of:\n(a) Uranium\n(b) Thorium\n(c) Titanium\n(d) Beryllium\nCorrect Answer: (b) Thorium [Explanation: Monazite beach sand contains rich concentrations of Thorium and rare earth elements, vital for the third stage of India's nuclear power programme.]"
