    "topic_title": "Demographic Profile & Tribal Communities of Andhra Pradesh",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q3. How many tribal communities in Andhra Pradesh are officially designated by the Government of India as Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs)?\n(a) 4\n(b) 7\n(c) 12\n(d) 15\nCorrect Answer: (b) 7 [Explanation: Andhra Pradesh has 7 designated PVTGs: Chenchus, Konda Reddis, Kolams, Khonds, Porjas, Savaras, and Gadabas.]"
