    "topic_title": "Demographic Profile & Tribal Communities of Andhra Pradesh",
    "subject_title": "Geography of India & Andhra Pradesh",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Which district in residual Andhra Pradesh holds the highest population density per square kilometer according to the 2011 Census?\n(a) Visakhapatnam\n(b) Krishna\n(c) Guntur\n(d) East Godavari\nCorrect Answer: (b) Krishna [Explanation: In the 2011 Census, Krishna district recorded the highest population density in the state at 518 persons per sq km, driven by fertile deltaic agriculture and urban centers.]"
