    "topic_title": "Emotional Intelligence: Dimensions, Utilities & Administrative Applications",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The ability to control impulsive reactions, suspend hasty judgments, and remain composed during high-stress crises corresponds to which dimension of EI?\n(a) Self-Awareness\n(b) Self-Regulation\n(c) Empathy\n(d) Extrinsic Motivation\nCorrect Answer: (b) Self-Regulation [Explanation: Self-regulation involves managing disruptive emotional impulses, maintaining composure, and acting rationally rather than reactively during crises.]"
