    "topic_id": "APPSC-G1-ETH-04",
    "topic_title": "Public Service Values & Ethics in Administration: Dilemmas & Codes",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "Q1. Which historic committee in the United Kingdom formulated the celebrated 'Seven Principles of Public Life' (including Selflessness and Integrity) in 1995?\n(a) Masterman Committee\n(b) Nolan Committee (Committee on Standards in Public Life)\n(c) Fulton Committee\n(d) Northcote-Trevelyan Committee\nCorrect Answer: (b) Nolan Committee (Committee on Standards in Public Life) [Explanation: Chaired by Lord Nolan, the Committee on Standards in Public Life (1995) established the seven foundational ethical principles for holders of public office.]"
