    "topic_id": "APPSC-G1-ETH-04",
    "topic_title": "Public Service Values & Ethics in Administration: Dilemmas & Codes",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "Q2. The administrative convention of 'Civil Service Anonymity', where the minister takes parliamentary responsibility while officials work behind the scenes, is rooted in the:\n(a) Westminster Model\n(b) Presidential System\n(c) French Prefect System\n(d) Soviet Nomenklatura\nCorrect Answer: (a) Westminster Model [Explanation: The British Westminster parliamentary system institutionalized civil service neutrality and anonymity to safeguard civil servants from political targeting.]"
