    "topic_title": "Probity in Governance, Transparency & Anti-Corruption Framework",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "**Q: Which committee report first recommended the formal establishment of the Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) in 1964?**\n* (a) Gorwala Committee on Public Administration\n* (b) Santhanam Committee on Prevention of Corruption\n* (c) Sarkaria Commission\n* (d) First Administrative Reforms Commission\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* The Committee on Prevention of Corruption, popularly known as the Santhanam Committee (1962–1964), recommended the setting up of the Central Vigilance Commission to tackle corruption in central government administration."
