    "topic_title": "Probity in Governance, Transparency & Anti-Corruption Framework",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "**Q: Under the Right to Information Act, 2005, what is the maximum time limit mandated for providing information if it concerns the life or liberty of a person?**\n* (a) 24 hours\n* (b) 48 hours\n* (c) 7 days\n* (d) 30 days\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* Section 7(1) of the RTI Act 2005 explicitly mandates that where the information sought concerns the life or liberty of a person, it must be provided within 48 hours of receipt of the request."
