    "topic_id": "APPSC-G1-ETH-06",
    "topic_title": "New Criminal Law Framework: BNS, BNSS & BSA 2023",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "**Q: Under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita (BNSS) 2023, for offences carrying what minimum punishment is forensic investigation and crime scene visit made mandatory?**\n* (a) 3 years or more\n* (b) 5 years or more\n* (c) 7 years or more\n* (d) Life imprisonment only\n* **Answer: (c)**\n* *Explanation:* Section 176(3) of the BNSS mandates that for any offence punishable with imprisonment of seven years or more, a forensic team must visit the crime scene to collect scientific evidence and record the process on video/audio-video electronic media."
