    "topic_title": "New Criminal Law Framework: BNS, BNSS & BSA 2023",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "**Q: Which former colonial offence under Section 124A of the Indian Penal Code (IPC) was replaced by provisions concerning 'acts endangering sovereignty, unity and integrity of India' in BNS?**\n* (a) Blasphemy\n* (b) Sedition\n* (c) Criminal Defamation\n* (d) Thuggee\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* Sedition under IPC Section 124A was repealed and replaced under Section 152 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), which penalizes acts endangering sovereignty, unity, and integrity of India rather than disaffection towards the government."
