    "topic_title": "Cyber Laws, Data Privacy & Taxation Framework",
    "subject_title": "Ethics and Law",
    "raw_text": "**Q: In the GST Council established under Article 279A of the Indian Constitution, what is the voting weight assigned to the Central Government and State Governments respectively?**\n* (a) Union: 50%, States: 50%\n* (b) Union: One-third (33.3%), States: Two-thirds (66.7%)\n* (c) Union: One-fourth (25%), States: Three-fourths (75%)\n* (d) Every State and Union has equal single vote\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* Under Article 279A(9), the vote of the Central Government has a weightage of one-third of the total votes cast, and the votes of all State Governments taken together have a weightage of two-thirds of the total votes cast. Every decision requires a majority of not less than three-fourths of the weighted votes."
