    "raw_text": "**Q: Under the Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code (IBC) 2016, which authority serves as the Adjudicating Authority for corporate insolvency resolution processes?**\n* (a) Debt Recovery Tribunal (DRT)\n* (b) National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT)\n* (c) High Court of the respective state\n* (d) Serious Fraud Investigation Office (SFIO)\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* The National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) is the designated Adjudicating Authority for Corporate Insolvency Resolution Processes (CIRP) and liquidation of corporate persons under the IBC 2016."
