    "raw_text": "**Q: When is the Reserve Bank of India considered to have failed in meeting the statutory inflation target under the RBI Act 1934?**\n* (a) When inflation exceeds 6% in any single month\n* (b) When average inflation remains outside the 2%–6% band for two consecutive quarters\n* (c) When average inflation remains outside the 2%–6% band for three consecutive quarters\n* (d) When GDP growth drops below 4%\n* **Answer: (c)**\n* *Explanation:* Under Regulation 7 of the RBI Monetary Policy Committee Regulations, the RBI is deemed to have failed in maintaining the inflation target if the average headline CPI inflation is above the upper tolerance level of 6% or below 2% for any three consecutive quarters."
