    "raw_text": "**Q: What is the formula for calculating 'Primary Deficit' in government budgeting?**\n* (a) Fiscal Deficit - Revenue Deficit\n* (b) Fiscal Deficit - Interest Payments\n* (c) Total Expenditure - Total Receipts\n* (d) Revenue Receipts - Capital Expenditure\n* **Answer: (b)**\n* *Explanation:* Primary Deficit is calculated as Fiscal Deficit minus Net Interest Payments. It indicates the government borrowing required to finance expenditures other than legacy interest obligations."
