    "topic_title": "Fiscal Policy, Public Debt & FRBM Framework",
    "subject_title": "Economy - India & AP",
    "raw_text": "**Q: What combined General Government Debt-to-GDP ratio was recommended by the N.K. Singh FRBM Review Committee to be achieved?**\n* (a) 40% of GDP\n* (b) 50% of GDP\n* (c) 60% of GDP (40% Centre, 20% States)\n* (d) 75% of GDP\n* **Answer: (c)**\n* *Explanation:* The N.K. Singh Committee (2017) recommended a combined debt-to-GDP target of 60% by 2022-23, comprising 40% for the Central Government and 20% for State Governments."
