    "topic_title": "Fiscal Policy, Public Debt & FRBM Framework",
    "subject_title": "Economy - India & AP",
    "raw_text": "**Q: Which of the following is categorized as 'Capital Expenditure' in the Union Budget?**\n* (a) Payment of salaries to government employees\n* (b) Subsidies on food and fertilizers\n* (c) Loans and advances given to State Governments\n* (d) Interest payments on market debt\n* **Answer: (c)**\n* *Explanation:* Loans and advances disbursed to State Governments and Union Territories create financial assets and are therefore classified as Capital Expenditure. Salaries, subsidies, and interest payments are recurring Revenue Expenditures."
