    "topic_title": "Logical Reasoning, Analytical Ability, Syllogisms & Seating Arrangements",
    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "Q5. Seven persons A, B, C, D, E, F, and G are sitting in a straight row facing North. C is sitting fourth to the right of G. Neither C nor G sits at any extreme end. A is sitting second to the left of C. Who is sitting exactly at the center (4th position) of the row?\n(a) A\n(b) B\n(c) D\n(d) C\nCorrect Answer: (a) A [Explanation: In a row of 7 seats (1 to 7). G and C are not at ends, and C is 4th to the right of G (meaning C index = G index + 4). Since G >= 2 and C <= 6: G must be at seat 2, which places C at seat 2 + 4 = 6. A is 2nd to the left of C, so A is at seat 6 - 2 = 4 (the exact center of the row).] "
