    "raw_text": "Q2. In a certain code language, 'ROBUST' is coded as 'QNATRS'. How is 'ZYXWVU' coded in that language?\n(a) YXWVUT\n(b) YXWVTR\n(c) AYXWVU\n(d) YZWVUT\nCorrect Answer: (a) YXWVUT [Explanation: In ROBUST -> QNATRS, each letter is shifted by -1 backward in the alphabet: R-1=Q, O-1=N, B-1=A, U-1=T, S-1=R, T-1=S. Applying -1 to ZYXWVU gives Z-1=Y, Y-1=X, X-1=W, W-1=V, V-1=U, U-1=T, resulting in YXWVUT.]"
