    "raw_text": "Four electronic traffic signals at four distinct intersections in Vijayawada change their lights every 30 seconds, 45 seconds, 60 seconds, and 90 seconds respectively. If all four signals change simultaneously at 8:00 AM, at what time will they next change simultaneously? Formulate the LCM prime factorization model. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Simultaneous synchronization occurs at the Least Common Multiple (LCM) of the individual cycle intervals. Given intervals: 30s, 45s, 60s, 90s.\nPrime factorization:\n30 = 2^1 * 3^1 * 5^1\n45 = 3^2 * 5^1\n60 = 2^2 * 3^1 * 5^1\n90 = 2^1 * 3^2 * 5^1\nLCM = 2^max(1,0,2,1) * 3^max(1,2,1,2) * 5^max(1,1,1,1) = 2^2 * 3^2 * 5^1 = 4 * 9 * 5 = 180 seconds.\nConvert seconds to minutes: 180 seconds / 60 = 3 minutes.\nTherefore, the signals will next change simultaneously at 8:00 AM + 3 minutes = 8:03 AM."
