    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "A sum of money invested at compound interest doubles itself in 5 years. In how many years will it become 8 times of itself at the same rate of interest? Prove using exponential compounding equations. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: Let principal be P and rate be R. Amount after 5 years = 2P. Using compounding formula: 2P = P(1 + R/100)^5 => (1 + R/100)^5 = 2. We need amount to become 8 times, so A = 8P. 8P = P(1 + R/100)^T => (1 + R/100)^T = 8 = 2^3. Substitute 2 = (1 + R/100)^5: (1 + R/100)^T = [ (1 + R/100)^5 ]^3 = (1 + R/100)^15. Equating bases and exponents: T = 15 years. Thus, the money will become 8 times in exactly 15 years."
