    "subject_title": "General Mental and Psychological Abilities",
    "raw_text": "A and B can complete a project in 12 days, B and C in 15 days, and C and A in 20 days. How long will they take to complete the project working all together? If A leaves after 4 days of joint work, in how many more days will B and C finish the remainder? Formulate the unitary efficiency breakdown. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: 1. Total Work = LCM(12, 15, 20) = 60 units. 2. Efficiency equations: (A + B) = 60/12 = 5 units/day; (B + C) = 60/15 = 4 units/day; (C + A) = 60/20 = 3 units/day. Sum of equations: 2(A + B + C) = 5 + 4 + 3 = 12 => Combined (A + B + C) = 6 units/day. Days together = 60 / 6 = 10 days. 3. Remaining work: In first 4 days together, work done = 4 * 6 = 24 units. Remaining work = 60 - 24 = 36 units. Since A leaves, B and C continue together with combined rate of 4 units/day. Additional time required = 36 / 4 = 9 days."
