    "raw_text": "Question: Is the integer x divisible by 6?\nStatement I: x is divisible by 3.\nStatement II: x is divisible by 4.\nEvaluate the data sufficiency step-by-step and determine whether statements alone or together suffice. (APPSC Group-1 Mains Analytical, 10 Marks)\n-> Model Approach: To be divisible by 6, x must be divisible by both 2 and 3. Statement I tells us x is divisible by 3 (e.g., x=9, not divisible by 6; x=12, divisible by 6) -> Insufficient. Statement II tells us x is divisible by 4 (meaning x is divisible by 2 and an even multiple of 4; e.g., x=8, not divisible by 6; x=12, divisible by 6) -> Insufficient. Combining Statements I and II: x is divisible by both 3 and 4. Since 3 and 4 are co-prime, x must be divisible by LCM(3, 4) = 12. Every multiple of 12 is necessarily a multiple of 6 (12 = 6 * 2). Thus, both statements together are SUFFICIENT to answer the question definitively."
